-- The port's additions to Cloudberry's init files for its resource group
-- tests (init_file_resgroup), read by gpdiff.pl after them.

-- start_matchsubs

# A group's memory in gp_resgroup_status_per_host, which is what its
# cgroup's memory.current says: what processes that ran in the group, or
# were moved into it, charged there, until the kernel takes it back.  A
# dropped group's idle sessions are moved into default_group, as
# Cloudberry's cgroup code moves them, and charge it some as they end; so
# resgroup_views finds default_group, idle, with a little.  That figure is
# made one; the CPU beside it is compared.
m/^ default_group \| 6437    \| \d+\.\d\d      \| \d+\.\d\d +$/
s/\| \d+\.\d\d +$/| (memory)/

-- end_matchsubs
